# Public documentation (banaoo.in/docs)

Customer-facing docs live under `src/content/docs/`:

- **Manifest:** `src/content/docs/registry.ts` — titles, slugs, `lastUpdated`
- **Articles:** `src/content/docs/articles/<slug>.md` — markdown body
- **Routes:** `/docs`, `/docs/:slug` — do not break slugs without redirects

## When to update docs

If your change affects something a restaurant owner would see or configure, update the matching article **in the same task/PR**:

| Area changed | Update article |
|--------------|----------------|
| Auth, onboarding, account | `getting-started.md` |
| Outlets, menu, QR menus | `outlets-and-menu.md` |
| Orders, POS, self-service, discounts | `orders-and-pos.md` |
| Kitchen KDS, sounds, statuses | `kitchen.md` |
| Bills, GST, reprints | `billing-and-receipts.md` |
| Printer fleet, native print, ESC/POS, routing | `printers.md` |
| Android APK, Bluetooth, permissions | `mobile-app.md` |
| Errors, support flows | `faq-troubleshooting.md` |

## How to update

1. Edit the relevant `.md` file — plain language for owners, no secrets or internal paths.
2. Bump `lastUpdated` for that article in `registry.ts` (ISO date `YYYY-MM-DD`).
3. If you add a new topic, add a `DOC_ARTICLES` entry and create `articles/<slug>.md`.

## Checklist (team releases)

- [ ] Public docs updated: `src/content/docs/articles/...`
- [ ] `lastUpdated` bumped in `registry.ts`

Do not put `.env`, API keys, or full internal changelogs in public docs.
